{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'ls -R poc/data/judging-v13s-blind6-2026-11-23 | head -120\nls -d poc/data/*blind[3456]*'","aggregated_output":"CHECKED.json\nE\nP-v8\nS\nTALLY.json\nadjudication\ncodex-writers.log\nreader-key.json\nreader-packets\nreasons.json\n\npoc/data/judging-v13s-blind6-2026-11-23/E:\nanswers\ncodex-writer.stream\nitem.json\nschema.json\nsystem.txt\nuser.txt\nwriter-prompt.txt\n\npoc/data/judging-v13s-blind6-2026-11-23/E/answers:\nclaude.json\ncodex.json\n\npoc/data/judging-v13s-blind6-2026-11-23/P-v8:\nanswers\ncodex-writer.stream\nitem.json\nschema.json\nsystem.txt\nuser.txt\nwriter-prompt.txt\n\npoc/data/judging-v13s-blind6-2026-11-23/P-v8/answers:\nclaude.json\ncodex.json\n\npoc/data/judging-v13s-blind6-2026-11-23/S:\nanswers\ncodex-writer.stream\nitem.json\nschema.json\nsystem.txt\nuser.txt\nwriter-prompt.txt\n\npoc/data/judging-v13s-blind6-2026-11-23/S/answers:\nclaude.json\ncodex.json\n\npoc/data/judging-v13s-blind6-2026-11-23/adjudication:\nX01.claude.json\nX01.codex.json\nX01.codex.stream\nX01.md\nX01.prompt.txt\nX06.claude.json\nX06.codex.json\nX06.codex.stream\nX06.md\nX06.prompt.txt\nX08.claude.json\nX08.codex.json\nX08.codex.stream\nX08.md\nX08.prompt.txt\n\npoc/data/judging-v13s-blind6-2026-11-23/reader-packets:\nX01.claude.json\nX01.codex-prompt.txt\nX01.codex.json\nX01.codex.stream\nX01.md\nX02.claude.json\nX02.codex-prompt.txt\nX02.codex.json\nX02.codex.stream\nX02.md\nX03.claude.json\nX03.codex-prompt.txt\nX03.codex.json\nX03.codex.stream\nX03.md\nX04.claude.json\nX04.codex-prompt.txt\nX04.codex.json\nX04.codex.stream\nX04.md\nX05.claude.json\nX05.codex-prompt.txt\nX05.codex.json\nX05.codex.stream\nX05.md\nX06.claude.json\nX06.codex-prompt.txt\nX06.codex.json\nX06.codex.stream\nX06.md\nX07.claude.json\nX07.codex-prompt.txt\nX07.codex.json\nX07.codex.stream\nX07.md\nX08.claude.json\nX08.codex-prompt.txt\nX08.codex.json\nX08.codex.stream\nX08.md\ninterrupted\n\npoc/data/judging-v13s-blind6-2026-11-23/reader-packets/interrupted:\nX04.codex.json.empty\nX04.codex.stream\nX05.codex.json.empty\nX05.codex.stream\nX08.codex.json.empty\nX08.codex.stream\npoc/data/judging-v13s-blind3-2026-11-22\npoc/data/judging-v13s-blind4-2026-11-23\npoc/data/judging-v13s-blind5-2026-11-23\npoc/data/judging-v13s-blind6-2026-11-23\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '11565,11725p'\"","aggregated_output":" 11565\t      open in practice. A clean re-read does not turn D745 into a pass.\n 11566\t  - **The paid re-send stays on hold** until an E writer repair passes a clean $0 test. The proposed repair: the writer chooses between\n 11567\t    a forecast and \"can't tell\" before it assigns a discount, naming what makes one side more likely under its own assumptions. It is a\n 11568\t    new arm and goes to council before any send. Publishing management's figure whenever it sits on a cutoff would change the product,\n 11569\t    and needs Alex's own decision.\n 11570\t- **The question to Alex** (pending): \"资料没直接给出所问的数。用一个相关数字作比较，能解释为什么结果更可能在线的这一边，但另一边仍有可能。这时可以发布预测，还是要等到能从资料算出结果落在线的哪一边？\"\n 11571\t- **Not done.** Nothing was paid. Nothing was tuned on the 36 stored answers. The request was not changed after the registration.\n 11572\t\n 11573\t## D747 · 2026-11-23 · Alex rules that a forecast may rest on an explained indirect comparison\n 11574\t\n 11575\t- **The question** (after D746): \"资料没直接给出题目问的那个数，只能拿一个相关的数字来比。比如问四大云厂商今年的数据中心开支能不能过 7000 亿，资料只说“这四家 AI 基础设施开支超过 7300 亿”。这种比较能说明结果更可能落在线的某一边，但另一边也还有可能。这时系统可以发布预测吗，还是要等资料能直接算出落在哪边？\"\n 11576\t  - Options:\n 11577\t    - \"可以发布，要讲清楚 (推荐)\": the answer must explain why the comparison applies to the companies, the year and the quantity\n 11578\t      asked, and why, under its own assumptions, that side is more likely; an answer that cannot explain it is not supported;\n 11579\t    - \"先说“还判断不了”\";\n 11580\t    - \"先停在这里\".\n 11581\t- **Alex's answer** (2026-11-23): \"可以发布，要讲清楚 (推荐)\".\n 11582\t- **Decided (Alex).** When the passages do not give the asked quantity, a forecast may rest on a related figure. It is supported\n 11583\t  only when the answer explains two things: why the comparison applies to the companies, the period and the quantity asked; and why,\n 11584\t  under the answer's own stated assumptions, the chosen side of the line is more likely. An answer that cannot explain this is not\n 11585\t  supported.\n 11586\t  - D741 ruling 3 still holds: a total used for a narrower quantity states the deduction as its own figure, or gives a supported\n 11587\t    bound.\n 11588\t  - D745's ruling still holds: a justified unresolved answer counts as usable.\n 11589\t- **Next (D746).** The ruling's words go into the shared reader definitions (`blind_rules.py`). Then one $0 blinded re-read of nine\n 11590\t  stored answers, registered with its expected readings and reviewed by the council before any packet is read.\n 11591\t\n 11592\t## D748 · 2026-11-23 · The D747 re-read fails on a self-contradicting floor; three of four earlier splits settle under the ruling; council 63: ask Alex to authorize the E writer repair; the paid re-send stays on hold\n 11593\t\n 11594\t- **The result** (`docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND4-RESULT.md` §6; `REREAD-TALLY.json`, `reread-reasons.json`):\n 11595\t  - **FAIL on the stop line.** On U02 (S, Claude writer), both adjudicators upheld \"part above or added into its whole\". The answer\n 11596\t    calls \"more than $730B\" of AI infrastructure \"the supported floor\" for data-center spending, while its own total spending is $720B\n 11597\t    and its data-center outcome $705.6B.\n 11598\t    - The code did not catch it. The figure is linked only to the 98% share, and the floor is claimed in prose. D738 leaves that\n 11599\t      reading to readers.\n 11600\t    - In the 18 stored blind replies this explicit defect occurs once (Codex, council 63).\n 11601\t  - **Six of nine settle with compatible reasons**, and each fixed reading that settled matched its registration:\n 11602\t    - U01, U03 and U05: no;\n 11603\t    - U06: no;\n 11604\t    - U04 (justified unresolved): yes;\n 11605\t    - U08 ($25B deduction explained by the same companies' AI-infrastructure figure and Meta's share): yes.\n 11606\t  - **Three of the four answers that split in the targeted test now settle** (U04, U06, U08).\n 11607\t  - **Three splits remain:** T10, T15 and U02's support vote.\n 11608\t    - All six adjudicator votes followed their own family's first vote. Which family was stricter changed with the question: Codex on\n 11609\t      S, Claude on E.\n 11610\t    - T15 had been accepted in all three earlier readings.\n 11611\t- **A process error** (Claude and council 62). The registration required five boundary answers to settle, or to settle as expected,\n 11612\t  without estimating how often readers split on boundary answers (AGENTS §7.1, \"a conjunction over many items fails by chance\"). The\n 11613\t  stop on U02 does not depend on it.\n 11614\t- **Council round 63** (`claude-r63.md`, `codex-r63.md`) reached consensus:\n 11615\t  - **The FAIL stands. No further reader round.** Another vote on the same nine answers leaves the writers untouched.\n 11616\t  - **Claude conceded three points.**\n 11617\t    - The remaining splits are not shown to be random variation. T10 and T15 turn on judgement over \"explains why\" and \"more likely\".\n 11618\t      On U02, one side accepted the band and the other required the writer's stated route. D747 already rejects U02's route. No\n 11619\t      missing general clause was found.\n 11620\t    - A writer test with registered lines only on stable readings would let a repeat of U05's invented cut through. Each fresh E and\n 11621\t      S answer must earn agreement for its forecast or for its specific reason for \"can't tell\".\n 11622\t    - Changing the calculation format for prose-claimed bounds is deferred. One case does not establish it, and U08 shows that an\n 11623\t      indirect comparison must stay able to inform a forecast without becoming a binding minimum. U02 becomes a control instead.\n 11624\t  - **The recommendation.** Ask Alex to authorize the E writer repair despite the three disclosed splits. D746 made the repair\n 11625\t    conditional on reader agreement, so going ahead needs his decision.\n 11626\t    - The repair: the writer decides whether the evidence favours one side of the line before it chooses a discount. If it can\n 11627\t      explain only why sales might fall short, it says what remains unknown.\n 11628\t    - The changed request goes to the council before any send.\n 11629\t  - **The one test after approval.** A $0 blind test:\n 11630\t    - fresh Codex and Claude writers on E, S and P-v8;\n 11631\t    - the saved U05 and U02 mixed in as controls for an invented cut and an impossible floor.\n 11632\t    - To pass:\n 11633\t      - each fresh E and S answer earns agreement for its forecast or its specific \"can't tell\" reason;\n 11634\t      - both P-v8 answers are supported forecasts;\n 11635\t      - the code accepts the fresh replies;\n 11636\t      - no confirmed defect survives.\n 11637\t    - A settled unsupported answer or a contradictory floor fails. A persistent split is inconclusive. Only a clean result supports\n 11638\t      asking Alex for the paid re-send.\n 11639\t- **Not done.** Nothing was paid. No request text was changed.\n 11640\t\n 11641\t## D749 · 2026-11-23 · Alex authorizes the E writer repair and its $0 writer test\n 11642\t\n 11643\t- **The question** (after D748): \"下一步怎么走？\"\n 11644\t  - Options:\n 11645\t    - \"批准修写手再小测 (推荐)\": the writer first decides whether the evidence favours one side of the line, then whether to discount;\n 11646\t      if it can only say sales might fall short, it answers \"can't tell\" and says what is missing. The changed request goes to the\n 11647\t      council, then one $0 writer test on E, S and P with the two failed answers as controls. A clean pass comes back to Alex for the\n 11648\t      paid re-send.\n 11649\t    - \"不修，直接议花钱重发\".\n 11650\t    - \"先停在这里\".\n 11651\t- **Alex's answer** (2026-11-23): \"批准修写手再小测 (推荐)\".\n 11652\t- **Decided (Alex).** Repair the writer request as council 63 described. Review it in council before any send. Then run one $0\n 11653\t  blind writer test on E, S and P-v8, with the saved U05 (invented cut) and U02 (impossible floor) as reader controls, under D748's\n 11654\t  pass lines. The paid re-send stays on hold until that test passes clean.\n 11655\t\n 11656\t## D750 · 2026-11-23 · The D749 writer test is INCONCLUSIVE with no failed line; council 65 (under D439): one bullet-2 sentence on reaffirmed targets, then a second $0 writer test\n 11657\t\n 11658\t- **Alex's direction** (2026-11-23, before sleeping): \"你接下来开始自行收敛，方向吧，我要准备睡了，所以这边的决策交给你，还有 Council， 记得不要 Scope Drift， 我们的目标是把剩下有问题的地方收敛起来，然后准备要往 Production 方向去走了，所以你自己每次复习的时候看 Log， 看我们试过了哪些东西，不要犯一模一样的错误，然后赶紧的往收敛方向去做测量和把它定下来。\"\n 11659\t  - D439 governs: the council decides reversibly, no paid send (its ceiling is spent), nothing committed.\n 11660\t- **The result** (`docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND5-RESULT.md`; run `poc/data/judging-v13s-blind5-2026-11-23/`):\n 11661\t  - **The repair worked where it was aimed.**\n 11662\t    - E's Codex writer, which invented a cut in both earlier runs, now answers a justified unresolved, accepted by both families.\n 11663\t    - Both P-v8 replies are supported forecasts.\n 11664\t    - Both controls were caught: the invented cut settled no, and the impossible floor was upheld by both adjudicators.\n 11665\t    - No fresh defect, no refusal. S's Codex forecast is supported.\n 11666\t  - **Two splits:**\n 11667\t    - X05, E Claude, takes a not-yet-shipping target in full, asserting \"already selling at volume\". No passage shows shipments,\n 11668\t      revenue to date or orders.\n 11669\t    - X08, S Claude: one reader cites \"more than $730B\" as a floor above its own $710.4B outcome, the other reads it as a guide.\n 11670\t- **Claude's error, corrected.** I first recorded X08's reasons as compatible although my own note named the tension. Council 65\n 11671\t  caught it. X08 was then adjudicated as registered and stayed split.\n 11672\t- **Council round 65** (`claude-r65.md`, `codex-r65.md`) reached consensus:\n 11673\t  - X05's premise is a question of fact under the existing rule, not a gap in Alex's words.\n 11674\t  - Claude's closed list of \"volume in hand\" was rejected: it was wider and narrower than the standard at once.\n 11675\t  - The smaller sentence is at bullet 2: \"it remains a forecast when reaffirmed, and is taken in full only when you show what evidence\n 11676\t    puts the required volume in hand for the period\".\n 11677\t  - One $0 writer test on all three cases (Alex's three-case condition), with the same controls and lines. On S, a reading that cites a\n 11678\t    floor above the answer's own outcome is not compatible with one that reads a guide.\n 11679\t  - The paid re-send stays on hold.\n 11680\t- **Done.** The sentence was changed (4,794 → 4,867 characters). Cases 111 of 111, rehearsal 19 of 19, pinned plan unchanged. The test\n 11681\t  is registered (`SMALL-DESIGN.md` §5 [D750]) and built by `blind6.py`. Council round 66 reviews it before any send.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
